From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:36:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] api/call-link-join: keep the group update that follows the
 join ACK

A call link's link_join ACK and the group_update right after it carry the
same transaction-id: the ACK has no relay and no device PID, the update has
both and, for the account that joined second, rekey=1. applyGroupUpdate
dropped it as an already held transaction, so that account never installed
the relay or PIDs and never fanned the group key out; maybeStartMedia waited
for the key forever (no "starting media", 0 frames each way in the logs).
A same-transaction update is now kept when it adds the relay or PIDs the held
one lacks.

Validated: group_update_carry_test.go (the decision table) and
engine_call_link_test.go (ACK then the full update: applied; again: stale;
fails without the change). Not yet on a live call.
---
