 engine_call_link_test.go   | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 engine_group_control.go    | 16 +++++++++--
 group_update_carry.go      | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++
 group_update_carry_test.go | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 147 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 6fb061d..d7a44d5 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -22,6 +22,15 @@ All notable changes to meowcaller, tracked per module. Format loosely follows
   they are a guest (`account_kind=guest`): a guest has no phone number, so
   the name is all a client can show.
 - Joining a link whose call is already held here is refused.
+- A link's join ACK and the `group_update` right after it carry the same
+  transaction-id: the ACK has no relay and no device PID, the update has both
+  and asks the account that joined second for the group key (`rekey="1"`).
+  The update was dropped as already held, so that account never got the relay
+  or sent the key and the call stayed silent. A same-transaction update is
+  now kept when it adds the relay or PIDs the held one lacks
+  (`groupUpdateIsStale`; `engine_call_link_test.go`, `group_update_carry_test.go`).
+  Such an update does not make this device draw a second key for a
+  transaction it already holds one for (`groupEpochHeldFor`).
 - KAT-verified on the captured stanzas (`signaling/call_link_test.go`,
   `engine_call_link_test.go`); not yet validated on a live call.
 
